After upgrading NCCL from 2.28 to 2.29, SymmetricMemory reports the following error:
$ pytest -vs test/distributed/test_nccl.py -k NCCLSymmetricMemoryTest
...
torch.distributed.DistBackendError: NCCL error in: /pytorch/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/symm_mem/nccl_devcomm_manager.hpp:73, invalid usage (run with NCCL_DEBUG=WARN for details), NCCL version 2.29.2
ncclDevCommCreate failed

With NCCL 2.28, we were doing:
ncclDevCommRequirements reqs;
memset(&reqs, 0, sizeof(ncclDevCommRequirements));

NCCL 2.29 requires an initializer instead:
ncclDevCommRequirements reqs = NCCL_DEV_COMM_REQUIREMENTS_INITIALIZER;

Consider the following code:
import torch

def make_cl(n1, n2):
    def inner(x):
        return x + n1 + n2

    return inner

@torch.compile(backend="eager")
def fn(cl, x):
    return cl(x)

fn(make_cl(0, 1), torch.ones(3))
fn(make_cl(0, 2), torch.ones(3))
